# With its upkeep trigger on the stack, Mirrorweave makes the Doppelganger (a copy of the Kobolds) a green Bears until end of
# turn; the trigger then has it become a copy of the Bears, except it doesn't copy color, so it is green while Mirrorweave's
# copy is beneath. Once Mirrorweave ends at cleanup it is a blue Bears: color left uncopied is whatever the values beneath
# give, its own again, never a value fixed as it copied (CR 707.9c, 613.2a, 613.7).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Kobolds of Kher Keep
Vesuvan Doppelganger
Mirrorweave
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Grizzly Bears
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Kobolds of Kher Keep.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vesuvan Doppelganger.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mirrorweave.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears#1.Colors = Green
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears#2.Colors = Green
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Kobolds of Kher Keep.Colors = Red
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Colors = Blue
